  "term": "fight-or-flight response",
  "definition": "The fight-or-flight response is a rapid reaction to a stressor in which the body becomes physiologically activated to deal with threat. In the source packet, this response includes activation of the hypothalamic-pituitary axis and release of cortisol.",
